findings.body:
After the `if (num_keys < 0) { return; }` branch, the `else if (num_keys >= 0)` test is always true, so it reads as a condition when it is really just an `else`. The inner check is correct, since `pcmd->slot` is `INVALID_CLUSTER_SLOT` for zero keys and can only be `CLUSTER_CROSSSLOT` when there are keys. The condition should be a plain `else` so the intent is clear.

::suggestion{file="src/server.c" lines="4138-4147"}
if (num_keys < 0) {
    /* We skip the checks below since We expect the command to be rejected in this case */
    return;
}
/* Handle cross-slot keys: mark error and reset slot. */
if (pcmd->slot == CLUSTER_CROSSSLOT) {
    pcmd->read_error = CLIENT_READ_CROSS_SLOT;
    pcmd->slot = INVALID_CLUSTER_SLOT;
}
